# A genuinely FLAKY command: it emits one of several outcomes at random and
# occasionally exits non-zero. Even after normalization the payload differs,
# so litmus reports divergence. We disable timestamp/hex stripping here because
# the randomness is the *content*, not noise.
#
# Because randomness is real, `expect = flaky` asserts that we DO observe more
# than one distinct outcome across the runs.

name = flaky-random-outcome
description = Randomly prints one of several results and sometimes fails.
